{"body":"# Goal
Add a durable trusted staging primitive that reconstructs a canonical `hwm-task-context-pack/v1` from a small canonical `hwm-task-context-request/v1` and creates the exact `context.json` as an unattached Git blob in `Dsamofalov/hwm-context`, so downstream task-context publication no longer depends on large client/connector payload upload.

# Parent milestone
I09 Context compiler

# Lifecycle
`ready`

This remediation Issue is not claimed and creates no ownership branch until a separate implementation dialogue claims it.

# Why this prerequisite exists
Issue #48 proved a recurring production capability gap: a deterministic production pack can exceed the available client/connector inline payload limit, while the existing trusted I09-P2 publisher intentionally accepts an already materialized exact Git blob SHA and must not be widened retroactively into a large-byte transport. One-time upload through local files, `gh`, PATs, alternate runtimes, or manual object injection is not an acceptable production architecture.

Observed pre-remediation protected heads:
- `Dsamofalov/hwm-control/main`: `106718a5d0cf4db38afc9f365def883be27ffc76`;
- `Dsamofalov/hwm-context/main`: `4ab022337ff6e2cfa05c6bfdd5b0ac0b3ecfdd02`;
- `Dsamofalov/hwm_predictor/main`: `8fd669336b36064e842252d69fb4016cc526a9d4`.

Issue #48 remains claimed and paused on this remediation. #49 and #50 remain blocked downstream.

# Architecture boundary
Introduce separate forward-only versioned contracts:
- `hwm-task-context-stage-request/v1`;
- `hwm-task-context-stage-result/v1`.

Do not retroactively change:
- `hwm-task-context-publish-request/v1`;
- `hwm-task-context-publish-result/v1`;
- merged I09-P0 task-context request/pack semantics;
- historical-ledger publisher schemas/boundary;
- bootstrap publisher schemas/boundary.

Transport remains trusted `Dsamofalov/hwm-context` Issue #27 with the existing exact author allowlist.

The stage request carries a validated canonical `hwm-task-context-request/v1` plus expected request/context identities. It must not transport large generated `context.json` bytes.

The trusted staging workflow must:
- execute only trusted compiler/provider code from protected `Dsamofalov/hwm-control/main` and trusted staging code from protected `Dsamofalov/hwm-context/main`;
- never execute candidate branch/PR code or generated context content;
- independently observe and verify exact protected control/context/product heads;
- independently verify the bound GitHub Issue snapshot, deterministic project-state snapshot, historical-ledger commit/blob/content identities, and every explicit Knowledge Delta blob/content identity;
- run the deterministic compiler at least twice from identical validated inputs and require byte equality;
- require expected `request_id`, canonical request SHA-256, canonical `context.json` SHA-256, and calculated Git blob SHA-1 to match the stage request expectations;
- enforce the existing public-data validation boundary;
- reject any accepted pack larger than the current task-context `MAX_BLOB_BYTES` bound;
- create only an unattached Git blob in the `Dsamofalov/hwm-context` object database;
- create or modify no refs, branches, PRs, default branch, protected `main`, reviews, merges, approvals, or required statuses;
- use only repository-scoped short-lived built-in `GITHUB_TOKEN` permissions required for object creation and transport result publication;
- use no PAT, deploy key, GitHub App secret, user-provided secret, or long-lived credential;
- implement exact idempotency and concurrency semantics so an exact replay returns the immutable prior successful result and a reused request identity with different normalized payload fails closed;
- return a normalized `hwm-task-context-stage-result/v1` binding exact blob/content/request/compiler provenance.

The existing task-context publisher must remain unchanged and subsequently consume the returned `blob_sha` through its existing `hwm-task-context-publish-request/v1` contract.

# Required live acceptance
Use a disposable public-disclosure-safe task-context request whose generated canonical pack is larger than the currently observed connector/tool payload limit.

Acceptance must prove:
- exact deterministic compilation from independently verified authoritative inputs;
- a second independent compilation is byte-identical;
- successful unattached Git blob creation in `Dsamofalov/hwm-context`;
- returned Git blob SHA equals the independently calculated exact Git blob SHA;
- the created blob can be read back and is byte-exact with the compiled canonical `context.json`;
- the unchanged existing task-context publisher can consume that staged blob in a disposable protected PR flow, with exact candidate-head CI and trusted strict status according to the existing I09-P2 boundary;
- disposable publication is closed/cleaned without production materialization.

Required live negative cases must fail closed without forbidden mutation:
- unauthorized author;
- malformed stage request;
- stale protected control/context/product head;
- stale or mismatched GitHub Issue snapshot;
- stale or mismatched deterministic project-state binding;
- stale or mismatched historical-ledger binding;
- stale or mismatched Knowledge Delta binding;
- wrong expected request hash/identity;
- wrong expected context SHA-256;
- wrong expected Git blob SHA;
- unsafe/public-data-violating content;
- generated pack larger than `MAX_BLOB_BYTES`;
- any request that attempts to bind or execute candidate-code refs instead of protected trusted code.

After acceptance prove:
- protected `hwm-context/main` did not change except through an explicitly required implementation protected PR;
- no staging job created publication refs/branches/PRs/statuses;
- no disposable publication refs remain after cleanup;
- active rulesets, strict required status provenance, branch protection, historical publisher boundary, and existing task-context publisher contract remain unchanged/weakened by zero.

# hwm-control completion requirements
The remediation implementation must complete through protected repository flows.

In `Dsamofalov/hwm-control`:
- add the forward-only stage contract schemas, architecture/contract documentation, deterministic contract/runtime tests as applicable, `BUILD_STATUS.json` completion bookkeeping, and canonical Knowledge Delta for this remediation task;
- protected PR-head Infrastructure CI must pass;
- guarded protected merge must succeed;
- exact post-merge Infrastructure CI must pass.

After the final protected `hwm-control/main` for the remediation is known, rematerialize canonical `state/current.json` through the existing deterministic project-state semantics on that final protected main. The final materialized state must reflect:
- this remediation task completed;
- `I09-0048` still claimed;
- Issue #49 blocked;
- Issue #50 blocked;
- no fabricated downstream readiness/ownership.

If `Dsamofalov/hwm-context` implementation changes are required, they must likewise use a protected implementation PR with exact PR-head Repository Bootstrap CI, guarded protected merge, and exact post-merge Repository Bootstrap CI. Final protected-main bytes and ruleset state must be reverified.

# Dependencies
None. This remediation is READY and is the sole new prerequisite blocking completion of Issue #48.

# Downstream DAG
- Issue #48 remains `claimed` and depends on completion of this remediation.
- Issue #49 remains `blocked` on #48.
- Issue #50 remains `blocked` on #49.
- Do not claim #48/#49/#50 from this remediation dialogue.

# Non-goals / forbidden
- No one-time manual production blob upload as the solution.
- No local-file/`gh`/PAT/deploy-key/GitHub-App-secret workaround.
- No product repository mutation.
- No LLM/OpenAI API use.
- No semantic wiki synthesis or Graphify.
- No direct push to protected `main`.
- No widening of existing task-context publish request/result schemas.
- No publisher merge/approval/status authority.
- No staging ref/branch/PR creation authority.

# Done when
- stage request/result v1 contracts are merged and protected;
- trusted compiler-backed staging implementation is merged and protected;
- live disposable acceptance proves large-pack staging, exact readback, unchanged-publisher consumption, negative matrix, cleanup, and unchanged ruleset/security boundaries;
- both affected repositories have exact required PR-head and post-merge CI evidence;
- `BUILD_STATUS.json`, canonical remediation Knowledge Delta, and rematerialized `state/current.json` are merged on protected hwm-control main;
- Issue #48 can independently observe the remediation as completed and then regenerate a fresh authoritative request/pack identity from the new protected heads.","title":"I09-P2 remediation: Add trusted compiler-backed task-context blob staging"}
